      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description : "1.182 RHEL-10-500205"
      info        : "RHEL 10 must notify the system administrator (SA) and information system security officer (ISSO) (at a minimum) when allocated audit record storage volume 75 percent utilization.

GROUP ID: V-281113RULE ID: SV-281113r1184746

If security personnel are not notified immediately when storage volume reaches 75 percent utilization, they are unable to plan for audit record storage capacity expansion."
      solution    : "Configure RHEL 10 to initiate an action to notify the SA and ISSO (at a minimum) when allocated audit record storage volume reaches 75 percent of the repository maximum audit record storage capacity by adding/modifying the following line in the \"/etc/audit/auditd.conf\" file.

space_left_action = email

Restart the audit daemon with the following command for the changes to take effect:

$ sudo service auditd restart"
      reference   : "800-171|3.3.4,800-171r3|03.03.04,800-53|AU-5(1),800-53r5|AU-5(1),CAT|II,CCI|CCI-001855,CN-L3|7.1.3.7(e),CSF|PR.PT-1,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(b),ITSG-33|AU-5(1),LEVEL|2A,NESA|T3.3.1,QCSC-v1|8.2.1,QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-281113r1184746_rule,STIG-ID|RHEL-10-500205,TBA-FIISB|37.3.2,Vuln-ID|V-281113"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/26403"
