    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.419 RHEL-10-800180"
      info        : "RHEL 10 must limit the number of bogus Internet Control Message Protocol (ICMP) response errors logs.

GROUP ID: V-281350RULE ID: SV-281350r1167200

Some routers will send responses to broadcast frames that violate RFC-1122, which fills up a log file system with many useless error messages. An attacker may take advantage of this and attempt to flood the logs with bogus error logs. Ignoring bogus ICMP error responses reduces log size, although some activity would not be logged.

Satisfies: SRG-OS-000420-GPOS-00186, SRG-OS-000142-GPOS-00081"
      solution    : "Configure RHEL 10 to not log bogus ICMP errors.

Create a configuration file if it does not already exist:

$ sudo vi /etc/sysctl.d/ipv4_icmp_ignore_bogus_error_responses.conf

Add the following line to the file:

net.ipv4.icmp_ignore_bogus_error_responses = 1

Reload settings from all system configuration files with the following command:

$ sudo sysctl --system"
      reference   : "800-171|3.13.1,800-171r3|03.13.01,800-53|SC-5,800-53|SC-7(4),800-53r5|SC-5a.,800-53r5|SC-7(4),CAT|II,CCI|CCI-001105,CCI|CCI-002385,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(j),CSF|DE.CM-1,CSF|PR.AC-5,CSF|PR.DS-4,CSF|PR.PT-4,CSF2.0|DE.CM-01,CSF2.0|PR.DS-01,CSF2.0|PR.DS-02,CSF2.0|PR.DS-10,CSF2.0|PR.IR-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.14,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.16,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.20,ISO/IEC-27001|A.13.1.3,ITSG-33|SC-5,ITSG-33|SC-5a.,ITSG-33|SC-7(4),LEVEL|2A,NESA|T3.3.1,NESA|T4.5.4,NIAv2|GS1,NIAv2|GS2a,NIAv2|GS2b,NIAv2|GS8e,NIAv2|GS10c,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|1.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|1.2,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|1.2.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|1.3,PCI-DSSv4.0|1.2.1,PCI-DSSv4.0|1.4.1,QCSC-v1|5.2.1,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|6.2,QCSC-v1|8.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-281350r1167200_rule,STIG-ID|RHEL-10-800180,TBA-FIISB|43.1,Vuln-ID|V-281350"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/26403"
