    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description : "1.7 RHEL-10-000560"
      info        : "RHEL 10 must use a separate file system for \"/var/log\".

GROUP ID: V-280940RULE ID: SV-280940r1184730

Placing \"/var/log\" in its own partition enables better separation between log files and other files in \"/var/\"."
      solution    : "Configure RHEL 10 to use a separate file system for log file directories by migrating the \"/var/log\" path onto a separate file system."
      reference   : "800-53|SC-5,800-53r5|SC-5a.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-002385,CSF|DE.CM-1,CSF|PR.DS-4,CSF2.0|DE.CM-01,CSF2.0|PR.IR-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|SC-5,ITSG-33|SC-5a.,LEVEL|2A,NESA|T3.3.1,NIAv2|GS8e,NIAv2|GS10c,QCSC-v1|8.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-280940r1184730_rule,STIG-ID|RHEL-10-000560,Vuln-ID|V-280940"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/26403"
