    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description : "1.8 RHEL-10-000570"
      info        : "RHEL 10 must use a separate file system for \"/var/tmp\".

GROUP ID: V-280941RULE ID: SV-280941r1184731

The \"/var/tmp\" partition is used as temporary storage by many programs. Placing \"/var/tmp\" in its own partition enables the setting of more restrictive mount options, which can help protect programs that use it."
      solution    : "Configure RHEL 10 to use a separate file system for the \"/var/tmp\" path by migrating \"/var/tmp\" onto a separate file system."
      reference   : "800-53|SC-5,800-53r5|SC-5a.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-002385,CSF|DE.CM-1,CSF|PR.DS-4,CSF2.0|DE.CM-01,CSF2.0|PR.IR-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|SC-5,ITSG-33|SC-5a.,LEVEL|2A,NESA|T3.3.1,NIAv2|GS8e,NIAv2|GS10c,QCSC-v1|8.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-280941r1184731_rule,STIG-ID|RHEL-10-000570,Vuln-ID|V-280941"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/26403"
      file        : "/etc/fstab"
      regex       : "^[^#\\n\\r]+[\\s]+/var/tmp[\\s]+"
